    "body": "## Motivation\nCached follow-ups can exhaust a single-pool KV cache while a long prompt is still mid-chunked-prefill. The scheduler then forces a full chunk and raises `Prefill out of memory` even when less than one chunk is physically free.\n\nReproduced in production by SGLang-based deployments with 1.6M-token KV pools; free capacity at failure was 1,600–1,920 tokens while the forced continuation requested 8,192 tokens. Internal tracking: Coral-Bricks-AI/www#671.\n\n## Changes\n- Cap a single-pool continuation to page-aligned current capacity minus allocator page overhead.\n- Defer the continuation when no usable capacity remains.\n- Reserve its unfinished remainder against other requests admitted in the same pass.\n- Preserve existing SWA transient-window behavior.\n- Add focused budget and scheduler regressions.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #38655694487](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38655694487)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #38655694536](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38655694536)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #38655694542](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38655694542)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
